{"abstract":"Introduction: Older patients with cancer range from fit to frail with various comorbidities and resilience to chemotherapy. Besides nausea and fatigue, a significant number of patients experience dizziness and impaired walking balance after chemotherapy, which can have great impact on their functional ability and health related quality of life. Symptoms are easily overlooked and therefore often underreported and managed, which is why symptoms could end up as long-lasting side effects. The aim of this study is to investigate the development of dizziness, decline in walking balance, and sarcopenia and the effect of a comprehensive geriatric assessment and 12 weeks of group-based exercise on these symptoms. The exercise intervention includes vestibular and balance exercises, and progressive resistance training, to counteract the symptoms in older patients with colorectal cancer treated with chemotherapy. Materials and Methods: This is a randomized controlled trial including patients ≥65 years initiating (neo)adjuvant or first-line palliative chemotherapy for colorectal cancer. Patients will undergo a comprehensive assessment program including measures of vestibular function, balance, muscle strength, mass, and endurance, peripheral and autonomic nerve function, and subjective measures of dizziness, concern of falling, and health related quality of life. Tests will be performed at baseline, 12, and 24 weeks. Patients will be placed in three different randomized controlled trials depending on chemotherapy regimen and randomized 1:1 to comprehensive geriatric assessment and exercise three times/week or control. Participants in both groups will continue with usual care, including standardized oncological treatment. In total, 150 patients are needed to assess the two primary outcomes of (1) maintenance of walking balance assessed with Dynamic Gait Index and (2) lower limb strength and endurance assessed with 30 Second Sit-to-Stand Test at 12 weeks. The primary outcomes will be analyzed using a mixed linear regression model investigating the between-group differences. Discussion: Trial enrollment began in April 2023 and is the first trial to evaluate reasons for dizziness, decline in walking balance, and sarcopenia in older patients receiving chemotherapy. The trial will provide new and valuable knowledge in how to assess, manage, and prevent dizziness, decline in walking balance, and sarcopenia in older patients with colorectal cancer. Trial Registration: The Regional Ethics Committee (j.nr. H-22064206). Danish Data Protection Agency (P-2023-86) and ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT05710809).","author_count":10,"contributors":["Piper, Katrine Storm","Suetta, Charlotte","Schou, Jakob Vasehus","Ryg, Jesper","Andersen, Hanne Elkjær","Langevad, Line Vind","Evering, Delaney","Mikkelsen, Marta Kramer","Lund, Cecilia Margareta","Christensen, Jan"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-735461"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Piper, Katrine Storm"],"keyword":["Chemotherapy","Colorectal cancer","Dizziness","Elderly","Geriatric oncology","Impaired walking","Older adults","Sarcopenia","Vertigo","Walking balance"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the save project sarcopenia and vertigo in aging patients with colorectal cancer a study protocol for three randomized controlled trials","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85190318886","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-735461","identifier":[{"id":"38631243","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85190318886","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2228d801-da7b-4023-9574-f8d0fece55ec","sdu-f0f4f225-774b-44be-ba92-466432e3957e"],"keyword":["Chemotherapy","Colorectal cancer","Dizziness","Elderly","Geriatric oncology","Impaired walking","Older adults","Sarcopenia","Walking balance","vertigo"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EE4044CAB4D1F7FD7D9E010AB2DEB5F8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Geriatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, AgeCare - Academy of Geriatric Cancer Research (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Geriatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Katrine Storm","key":"piperpau","last":"Piper","name":"Piper, Katrine Storm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Charlotte","key":"suettapau","last":"Suetta","locid":"26af20c6-3c1b-4b5a-aa41-bf3e1598e2b0","name":"Suetta, Charlotte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Vasehus","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","name":"Schou, Jakob Vasehus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"rygpau","last":"Ryg","locid":"c63490d8-ba13-4875-bf40-82c4aebbab6f","name":"Ryg, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8641-3062","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne Elkjær","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Hanne Elkjær","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line Vind","key":"langevadpau","last":"Langevad","name":"Langevad, Line Vind","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Delaney","key":"everingpau","last":"Evering","name":"Evering, Delaney","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Marta Kramer","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"33f85630-0d23-4898-b167-cc40ab71631f","name":"Mikkelsen, Marta Kramer","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Cecilia","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"1fb18e5b-7c88-43c0-9fa7-6c8a8668e75c","name":"Lund, Cecilia Margareta","name_org":"Lund, Cecilia","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jan","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38631243"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jgo.2024.101770","issn":["18794068","18794076"],"issn_org":["18794068"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Geriatric Oncology","paperid":"101770","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Geriatric Oncology","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85190318886"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2228d801-da7b-4023-9574-f8d0fece55ec","sdu-f0f4f225-774b-44be-ba92-466432e3957e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The SaVe project – Sarcopenia and Vertigo in aging patients with colorectal cancer : A study protocol for three randomized controlled trials","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-735461","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Aging is often associated with low-grade chronic inflammation and a senescent immune system. Vitamin D is a regulator of immune function, and low plasma vitamin D is associated with poor health. The association between plasma vitamin D and inflammatory biomarkers and risk of postoperative complications and survival in patients with colorectal cancer (CRC) is unknown. Our aim was to investigate these associations and how they are influenced by age. Materials and methods: Circulating vitamin D and the inflammatory biomarkers C-reactive protein (CRP), interleukin (IL)-6, and YKL-40 were measured in 398 patients with stage I–III CRC preoperatively. Older patients (≥70 years, n = 208) were compared to younger patients (<70 years, n = 190). The relation between vitamin D and complications and high inflammatory biomarker levels was presented by odds ratios ([OR], 95% confidence interval [CI]). Associations with survival were presented with hazard ratios ([HR], 95% CI). Results: Plasma vitamin D was higher in older patients than in younger patients (75 vs. 67 nmol/L, P = 0.001). High vitamin D was associated with low plasma CRP in younger patients (OR = 0.35, 95% CI 0.17–0.76), but not in older patients (OR = 0.93, 0.49–1.76). High vitamin D in older patients with CRC was associated with reduced risk of major complications (OR = 0.52, 0.28–0.95). This was not found in younger patients (OR = 1.47, 0.70–3.11). Deficient vitamin D (<25 nmol/L) was associated with short overall survival compared to sufficient (>50 nmol/L) irrespective of age (HR = 3.39, 1.27–9.37, P = 0.02). Conclusion: For patients with localized CRC, high vitamin D levels before resection were associated with reduced risk of high inflammatory biomarkers for younger patients and reduced risk of major postoperative complications for older patients. Vitamin D deficiency was associated with reduced survival regardless of age.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Dolin, Troels G.","Christensen, Ib J.","Lund, Cecilia Margareta","Bojesen, Stig E","Lykke, Jakob","Nielsen, Dorte Lisbet","Larsen, Jim S.","Johansen, Julia S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-492392"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CRP","Colorectal cancer","IL 6","Inflammation","Older patients","Postoperative Complications","Vitamin D","YKL 40"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preoperative plasma vitamin d in patients with localized colorectal cancer age dependent association with inflammation postoperative complications and survival","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-492392","identifier":[{"id":"36137882","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85138569811","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a5a4a6a3-f2c0-465f-ae10-91de417334bb"],"keyword":["CRP","Colorectal cancer","IL-6","Inflammation","Older patients","Postoperative complications","Vitamin D","YKL-40"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A6D07C93A32768D43D3FC8F38EBD0346"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Geriatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Troels G.","key":"dolinpau","last":"Dolin","name":"Dolin, Troels G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ib J.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Ib J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Cecilia M.","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"1fb18e5b-7c88-43c0-9fa7-6c8a8668e75c","name":"Lund, Cecilia Margareta","name_org":"Lund, Cecilia M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Stig E.","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","locid":"25f871c8-a69d-45d1-85b6-c438d7293b74","name":"Bojesen, Stig E","name_org":"Bojesen, Stig E.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob","key":"lykkepau","last":"Lykke","name":"Lykke, Jakob","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Dorte L.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8bd14092-b1da-4f24-b4db-d31d38f5f1b7","name":"Nielsen, Dorte Lisbet","name_org":"Nielsen, Dorte L.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jim S.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Jim S.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Julia S.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"b2f1fd05-1a2e-4879-b015-af4dfa479876","name":"Johansen, Julia S.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36137882"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejso.2022.08.040","issn":["07487983","15322157"],"issn_org":["07487983"],"issue":"1","journal":"European Journal of Surgical Oncology","pages":"244-251","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Surgical Oncology","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138569811"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a5a4a6a3-f2c0-465f-ae10-91de417334bb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Preoperative plasma vitamin D in patients with localized colorectal cancer : Age-dependent association with inflammation, postoperative complications, and survival","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-492392","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The association between pre-and perioperative inflammatory biomarkers, major compli-cations, and survival rates after resection of colorectal cancer (CRC) in older patients is largely unknown. The aim was to investigate age-dependent differences in these associations. Serum CRP, IL-6, and YKL-40 were measured preoperatively and on the first and second day after resection of CRC (stages I–III) in 210 older (≥70 years) and 191 younger patients (<70 years). The results from the complications was presented as an odds ratio (OR, with a 95% confidence interval (CI)) with logistic regression. Results from the mortality rates were presented as a hazard ratio (HR, with a 95% CI) using Cox proportional hazards regression. The preoperative inflammatory biomarkers were higher in the older vs. the younger patients. The risk of complications was increased in older patients with a high preoperative CRP (OR = 1.25, 95% CI 1.03–1.53), IL-6 (OR = 1.57, 95% CI 1.18–2.08), and YKL-40 (OR = 1.66, 95% CI 1.20–2.28), but not in younger patients. Mortality was higher in younger patients with high preoperative YKL-40 (HR = 1.66, 95% CI 1.06–2.60). This was not found in older patients. Elevated preoperative inflammatory biomarkers among older patients were associated with an increased risk of complications, but not mortality. Preoperative inflammatory biomarkers may be useful in assessing the risk of a complicated surgical course in older patients with CRC.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Dolin, Troels Gammeltoft","Christensen, Ib Jarle","Johansen, Astrid Zedlitz","Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","Jakobsen, Henrik Loft","Klein, Mads Falk","Lund, Cecilia Margareta","Bojesen, Stig E","Nielsen, Dorte Lisbet","Jensen, Benny Vittrup","Johansen, Julia S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-523444"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ageing","CRP","Colorectal cancer","Complications","IL 6","Inflammation","Inflammatory biomarkers","Surgery","YKL 40"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pre and perioperative inflammatory biomarkers in older patients resected for localized colorectal cancer associations with complications and prognosis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers14010161","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-523444","identifier":[{"id":"35008324","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85121806400","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8750535","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-d9a1656f-6dc3-472c-9a18-fbf2e1ddf0ca"],"keyword":["Ageing","CRP","Colorectal cancer","Complications","IL-6","Inflammation","Inflammatory biomarkers","Surgery","YKL-40"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E880844D9A5D390685033650FD3A873B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers14010161","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/289969248/cancers_14_00161_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Troels Gammeltoft","key":"dolintroelsgammeltoftpau","last":"Dolin","name":"Dolin, Troels Gammeltoft","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ib Jarle","key":"christensenibjarlepau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Ib Jarle","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Astrid Zedlitz","key":"johansenastridzedlitzpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Astrid Zedlitz","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans Jørgen","key":"nielsenhansjørgenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"87f9baf4-e29c-4104-be23-daf6d94d7124","name":"Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Loft","key":"jakobsenhenrikloftpau","last":"Jakobsen","name":"Jakobsen, Henrik Loft","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads Falk","key":"kleinmadsfalkpau","last":"Klein","locid":"bc2d812a-cb7e-4643-b00b-7cb615f73fb0","name":"Klein, Mads Falk","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cecilia Margareta","key":"lundceciliamargaretapau","last":"Lund","locid":"1fb18e5b-7c88-43c0-9fa7-6c8a8668e75c","name":"Lund, Cecilia Margareta","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stig Egil","key":"bojesenstigepau","last":"Bojesen","locid":"25f871c8-a69d-45d1-85b6-c438d7293b74","name":"Bojesen, Stig E","name_org":"Bojesen, Stig Egil","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dorte Lisbeth","key":"nielsendortelisbetpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8bd14092-b1da-4f24-b4db-d31d38f5f1b7","name":"Nielsen, Dorte Lisbet","name_org":"Nielsen, Dorte Lisbeth","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Benny Vittrup","key":"jensenbennyvittruppau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Benny Vittrup","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julia Sidenius","key":"johansenjuliaspau","last":"Johansen","locid":"b2f1fd05-1a2e-4879-b015-af4dfa479876","name":"Johansen, Julia S.","name_org":"Johansen, Julia Sidenius","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35008324"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/cancers14010161","issn":["20726694"],"issue":"1","journal":"Cancers","paperid":"161","status":"p","title":"Cancers","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121806400"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d9a1656f-6dc3-472c-9a18-fbf2e1ddf0ca"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pre-and perioperative inflammatory biomarkers in older patients resected for localized colorectal cancer : Associations with complications and prognosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-523444","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Arctic and subarctic ecosystems are experiencing substantial changes in hydrology, vegetation, permafrost conditions, and carbon cycling, in response to climatic change and other anthropogenic drivers, and these changes are likely to continue over this century. The total magnitude of these changes results from multiple interactions among these drivers. Field measurements can address the overall responses to different changing drivers, but are less capable of quantifying the interactions among them. Currently, a comprehensive assessment of the drivers of ecosystem changes, and the magnitude of their direct and indirect impacts on subarctic ecosystems, is missing. The Tornetrask area, in the Swedish subarctic, has an unrivalled history of environmental observation over 100 years, and is one of the most studied sites in the Arctic. In this study, we summarize and rank the drivers of ecosystem change in the Tornetrask area, and propose research priorities identified, by expert assessment, to improve predictions of ecosystem changes. The research priorities identified include understanding impacts on ecosystems brought on by altered frequency and intensity of winter warming events, evapotranspiration rates, rainfall, duration of snow cover and lake-ice, changed soil moisture, and droughts. This case study can help us understand the ongoing ecosystem changes occurring in the Tornetrask area, and contribute to improve predictions of future ecosystem changes at a larger scale. This understanding will provide the basis for the future mitigation and adaptation plans needed in a changing climate.","author_count":28,"contributors":["Pascual, Didac","Åkerman, Jonas","Becher, Marina","Callaghan, Terry V.","Christensen, Torben R.","Dorrepaal, Ellen","Emanuelsson, Urban","Giesler, Reiner","Hammarlund, Dan","Hanna, Edward","Hofgaard, Annika","Jin, Hongxiao","Johansson, Cecilia","Jonasson, Christer","Klaminder, Jonatan","Karlsson, Jan","Lundin, Erik","Michelsen, Anders","Olefeldt, David","Persson, Andreas","Phoenix, Gareth K.","Rączkowska, Zofia","Rinnan, Riikka","Ström, Lena","Tang, Jing","Varner, Ruth K.","Wookey, Philip","Johansson, Margareta"],"cuid":["S03-097.90-025753"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Pascual, Didac"],"country":["Canada","Norway","Poland","Russia","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Geological Survey of Sweden","Luleå University of Technology","Lund University","Norwegian Institute for Nature Research","Polish Academy of Sciences","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","Think Tank","Tomsk State University","Umeå University","University of Alberta","University of New Hampshire","University of Sheffield","University of Stirling","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Abiotic drivers","Arctic and subarctic","Biotic drivers","Ecosystem change","Ice","Permafrost","Research priorities","Responses","Snow cover","Sweden","Tundra","Vegetation","winter warming events"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the missing pieces for better future predictions in subarctic ecosystems a torneträsk case study","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s13280-020-01381-1","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Open access funding provided by Lund University. We are grateful to the Department of Physical Geography and Ecosystem Science, Lund University for the grant received to promote research integration and advancement of early-career researchers at the department 2018. We are also grateful to Göran Gustafsson Stiftelse for contributing with funding, and to Thomas Holst and Lars Eklundh for constructive comments on the design of the study. This study has been made possible by data provided by the Abisko Scientific Research Station and the Swedish Infrastructure for Ecosystem Science (SITES). MJ and TVC are very grateful for support by INTERACT funded through the EU Horizon2020 programme (GA 871120)."],"id":"S03-097.90-025753","identifier":[{"id":"32920769","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85090978576","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7782653","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000568974700002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-b39edbe8-1a55-4008-9f4c-0ff293e53054","dtu-25e46302-edf8-4755-a25f-3ab9a99f2bf7","ku-d8638408-93be-42dc-a8cc-c3756b449987"],"keyword":["ABISKO","Abiotic drivers","Arctic and subarctic","Biotic drivers","Ecosystem change","ICE","PERMAFROST","REGIONAL VARIABILITY","RESPONSES","Research priorities","SNOW COVER","SWEDEN","TUNDRA","VEGETATION","WINTER WARMING EVENTS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-A37694F1705CD951311D8EBAEE3BFCB8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/273668511/Pascual2021_Article_TheMissingPiecesForBetterFutur.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/249106160/Pascual2020_Article_TheMissingPiecesForBetterFutur.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/237837482/Pascual2021_Article_TheMissingPiecesForBetterFutur.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s13280-020-01381-1","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[