{"abstract":"Cerebral palsy (CP) is associated with cognitive impairments, learning difficulties and reduced social participation. Individual assessment is necessary for individually tailored interventions. This paper describes the development of a systematic follow-up programme of cognition, and the challenges of integrating it into the regular follow-up of children with CP. Initiated by the Nordic users‘ organisations, a group of psychologists proposed a protocol of follow-up of cognition in children with CP – the CP Cog. This protocol consists of neuropsychological instruments covering general cognitive functioning, visuospatial and executive functioning. The article presents a natural experiment describing development and implementation of the cognitive protocol in three Scandinavian countries. This introduction illustrates challenges associated with implementation, especially how the success of the protocol hinges on structural backup within the different countries. In conclusion the CP Cog assessment protocol holds the promise of increasing the awareness among habilitation professionals that children with CP are in need of cognitive evaluation and educational support.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bøttcher, Louise","Stadskleiv, Kristine","Berntsen, Torhild","Christensen, Klaus","Ödman, Pia","Korsfelt, Åsa","Kihlgren, Margareta"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-155090"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cerebral parese","Forebyggelse","Handicap","Handicappsykologi","Kognitionspsykologi","Kognitive vanskeligheder","indlæringsvanskeligheder"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"systematic cognitive monitoring of children with cerebral palsy the development of an assessment and follow up protocol","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84945218387","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-155090","identifier":[{"id":"84945218387","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2d057ccb-6a38-44ed-9bdf-3c8b36d282be"],"keyword":["Cerebral parese","Forebyggelse","Handicap","Handicappsykologi","Kognitionspsykologi","Kognitive vanskeligheder","indlæringsvanskeligheder"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D76B6A503927EDDFACEADD753111AE9A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Research Programme for Future Technologies, Culture and Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise","key":"bøttcherpau","last":"Bøttcher","locid":"7ce6dba0-0e80-4b35-a442-b89b28dfe956","name":"Bøttcher, Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6697-7274","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine","key":"stadskleivpau","last":"Stadskleiv","name":"Stadskleiv, Kristine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Torhild","key":"berntsenpau","last":"Berntsen","name":"Berntsen, Torhild","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Klaus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Pia","key":"ödmanpau","last":"Ödman","name":"Ödman, Pia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Åsa","key":"korsfeltpau","last":"Korsfelt","name":"Korsfelt, Åsa","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Margareta","key":"kihlgrenpau","last":"Kihlgren","name":"Kihlgren, Margareta","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/15017419.2015.1091035","issn":["15017419","17453011"],"issn_org":["15017419"],"issue":"4","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Disability Research","pages":"304-315","publisher":"Stockholm University Press","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Disability Research","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84945218387"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2d057ccb-6a38-44ed-9bdf-3c8b36d282be"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Systematic cognitive monitoring of children with cerebral palsy : the development of an assessment and follow-up protocol","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-155090","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Permafrost, a key component of the arctic and global climate system, is highly sensitive to climate change. Observed and ongoing permafrost degradation influences arctic hydrology, ecology and biogeochemistry, and models predict that rapid warming is expected to significantly reduce near-surface permafrost and seasonally frozen ground during the 21st century. These changes raise concern of how permafrost thaw affects the exchange of water and energy with the atmosphere. However, associated impacts of permafrost thaw on the surface energy balance and possible feedbacks on the climate system are largely unknown. In this study, we show that in northern subarctic Sweden, permafrost thaw and related degradation of peat plateaus significantly change the surface energy balance of three peatland complexes by enhancing latent heat flux and, to less degree, also ground heat flux at the cost of sensible heat flux. This effect is valid at all radiation levels but more pronounced at higher radiation levels. The observed differences in flux partitioning mainly result from the strong coupling between soil moisture availability, vegetation composition, albedo and surface structure. Our results suggest that ongoing and predicted permafrost degradation in northern subarctic Sweden ultimately result in changes in land-atmosphere coupling due to changes in the partitioning between latent and sensible heat fluxes. This in turn has crucial implications for how predictive climate models for the Arctic are further developed.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Stiegler, Christian","Johansson, Margareta","Christensen, Torben R.","Mastepanov, Mikhail","Lindroth, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-213225"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Climate change","Permafrost degradation","Surface energy balance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tundra permafrost thaw causes significant shifts in energy partitioning","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3402/tellusb.v68.30467","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-213225","identifier":[{"id":"84995642012","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9341949c-7c69-49de-b320-8bba2de7c686"],"keyword":["Climate change","Land- atmosphere coupling","Permafrost degradation","Subarctic peatlands","Surface energy balance"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-F6471C76AD627696196F98B6A46752D0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3402/tellusb.v68.30467","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/121897579/tellusb.v68.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Arctic Research Centre","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Arctic Ecosystem Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"stieglerpau","last":"Stiegler","name":"Stiegler, Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Margareta","key":"johanssonpau","last":"Johansson","name":"Johansson, Margareta","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben R","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"b6b7be53-7869-48a3-875e-76e6e85fc5a5","name":"Christensen, Torben R.","name_org":"Christensen, Torben R","orcid":"0000-0002-4917-148X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikhail","key":"mastepanovpau","last":"Mastepanov","locid":"c67f32e3-4371-4540-8423-075c24d524db","name":"Mastepanov, Mikhail","orcid":"0000-0002-5543-0302","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"lindrothpau","last":"Lindroth","name":"Lindroth, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3402/tellusb.v68.30467","issn":["02806509","16000889"],"issn_org":["02806509"],"issue":"1","journal":"Tellus B: Chemical and Physical Meteorology","paperid":"30467","publisher":"Stockholm University Press","status":"p","title":"Tellus B: Chemical and Physical Meteorology","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84995642012"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9341949c-7c69-49de-b320-8bba2de7c686"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Tundra permafrost thaw causes significant shifts in energy partitioning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-213225","year":"2016","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This study was initiated to analyze the effect of increased snow cover on plant photosynthesis in subarctic mires underlain by permafrost. Snow fences were used to increase the accumulation of snow on a subarctic permafrost mire in northern Sweden. By measuring reflected photosynthetic active radiation (PAR) the effect of snow thickness and associated delay of the start of the growing season was assessed in terms of absorbed PAR and estimated gross primary production (GPP). Six plots experienced increased snow accumulation and six plots were untreated. Incoming and reflected PAR was logged hourly from August 2010 to October 2013. In 2010 PAR measurements were coupled with flux chamber measurements to assess GPP and light use efficiency of the plots. The increased snow thickness prolonged the duration of the snow cover in spring. The delay of the growing season start in the treated plots was 18 days in 2011, 3 days in 2012 and 22 days in 2013. Results show higher PAR absorption, together with almost 35 % higher light use efficiency, in treated plots compared to untreated plots. Estimations of GPP suggest that the loss in early season photosynthesis, due to the shortening of the growing season in the treatment plots, is well compensated for by the increased absorption of PAR and higher light use efficiency throughout the whole growing seasons. This compensation is likely to be explained by increased soil moisture and nutrients together with a shift in vegetation composition associated with the accelerated permafrost thaw in the treatment plots.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bosio, Julia","Stiegler, Christian","Johansson, Margareta","Mbufong, Herbert Njuabe","Christensen, Torben R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-217482"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Stiegler, Christian"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Climate","Gross primary production","Light use efficiency","Long term","Nitrogen mineralization","Relative importance","Summer precipitation","THAWING PERMAFROST","alpine tundra"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"increased photosynthesis compensates for shorter growing season in subarctic tundra 000000000008 years of snow accumulation manipulations","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10584-014-1247-4","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-217482","identifier":[{"id":"84939969380","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000344387000012","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-9ab477fe-6437-4d06-a946-ffeb6fc6effe"],"keyword":["ALPINE TUNDRA","CLIMATE","GROSS PRIMARY PRODUCTION","LIGHT-USE EFFICIENCY","LONG-TERM","NITROGEN MINERALIZATION","RELATIVE IMPORTANCE","SUMMER PRECIPITATION","THAWING PERMAFROST","VEGETATION RESPONSES"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C2739DDA0F12C4CC9B29344E4D202F29"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10584-014-1247-4","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Arctic Research Centre, Arctic Research Centre - Arctic Research Centre, Roskilde","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Arctic Ecosystem Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Julia","key":"bosiopau","last":"Bosio","name":"Bosio, Julia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"stieglerpau","last":"Stiegler","name":"Stiegler, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Margareta","key":"johanssonpau","last":"Johansson","name":"Johansson, Margareta","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Herbert Njuabe","key":"mbufongpau","last":"Mbufong","locid":"848b560e-bdd9-4702-a336-913b48e7f67e","name":"Mbufong, Herbert Njuabe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben R.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"b6b7be53-7869-48a3-875e-76e6e85fc5a5","name":"Christensen, Torben R.","orcid":"0000-0002-4917-148X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10584-014-1247-4","issn":["01650009","15731480"],"issn_org":["01650009"],"issue":"2","journal":"Climatic Change","pages":"321-334","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media BV","publisher_org":"Springer Science and Business Media B.V.","status":"p","title":"Climatic Change","volume":"127"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84939969380"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9ab477fe-6437-4d06-a946-ffeb6fc6effe"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Increased photosynthesis compensates for shorter growing season in subarctic tundra-8 years of snow accumulation manipulations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-217482","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
